%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"background":"#ffffff","primaryColor":"#e8f1ff","primaryTextColor":"#1f2937","primaryBorderColor":"#3b82f6","lineColor":"#4b5563","secondaryColor":"#f1e8ff","tertiaryColor":"#fff7d6","fontFamily":"Arial, sans-serif"},"sequence":{"useMaxWidth":true,"diagramMarginX":25,"diagramMarginY":18,"actorMargin":34,"width":165,"height":60,"boxMargin":8,"messageMargin":24,"noteMargin":10}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Part as Active verified PART
    participant UI as MessageReactions (React)
    participant API as Forum, team chat, or DM route
    participant Service as Reaction service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (0067 functions)

    Note over UI,DB: Message lists already carry reaction counts from one batched summary per list.
    Part->>UI: Choose an approved reaction (pill or picker)
    UI->>UI: Show optimistic change and pause only this message
    UI->>API: PUT to add or DELETE to remove …/reactions/:code (no body)
    API->>API: Firebase, MFA, active, verified PART
    API->>API: Reactions enabled, approved code, 30 changes per minute
    API->>API: Conversation send guard (forum, team member, DM send access)
    API->>Service: Caller from session, message, reaction code
    Service->>DB: set_chat_message_reaction or set_direct_message_reaction
    DB->>DB: Recheck send rules, then insert-if-absent or delete
    DB-->>Service: changed true or false (repeat is a no-op)
    Service->>DB: Summarize this message
    DB-->>Service: count and reactedByMe per code
    Service-->>UI: Stored aggregate in the approved order
    UI-->>Part: Replace the optimistic change with server counts

    alt Feature off, message gone, denied, rate-limited, or server error
        API-->>UI: 404 FEATURE_DISABLED, safe 403/404, 429 with Retry-After, or 5xx
        UI-->>Part: Restore confirmed counts and show a short message, no automatic retry
    end

    Note over UI,DB: Responses never list who reacted. Reactions create no notifications,<br/>change no unread counts, and are not pushed in realtime.
